### Dataverse Web API — starter requests (REST Client extension)
### URL and token come from http/.env (git-ignored). Setup:
###   1. az login                          (once)
###   2. .\http\Get-DataverseToken.ps1     (creates .env from .env.example on first run;
###                                         set DATAVERSE_URL there, re-run when you get 401)
### Then click "Send Request" above any block.

@baseUrl = {{$dotenv DATAVERSE_URL}}
@apiVersion = v9.2
@token = {{$dotenv DATAVERSE_TOKEN}}

### WhoAmI — quick connectivity test
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/data/{{apiVersion}}/WhoAmI
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
OData-MaxVersion: 4.0
OData-Version: 4.0

### Retrieve top 5 accounts (select a few columns)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/data/{{apiVersion}}/accounts?$select=name,telephone1,revenue&$top=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
OData-MaxVersion: 4.0
OData-Version: 4.0

### Retrieve accounts with a filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/data/{{apiVersion}}/accounts?$select=name&$filter=revenue gt 100000&$orderby=name asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
OData-MaxVersion: 4.0
OData-Version: 4.0

### Create an account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/data/{{apiVersion}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
OData-MaxVersion: 4.0
OData-Version: 4.0

{
  "name": "Contoso Test Account",
  "telephone1": "555-0100"
}

### Update an account (replace GUID)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/data/{{apiVersion}}/accounts(00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000)
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
OData-MaxVersion: 4.0
OData-Version: 4.0

{
  "telephone1": "555-0199"
}
